# A filter must stay above a write-cast, otherwise it compares the value before the cast.

admin 'create table test::t20 { id: int4, a: int4 }'
---
> +---------+-------------+---------+-----------+
> |   id    |  namespace  |  table  |  created  |
> +---------+-------------+---------+-----------+
> |  16388  |    test     |   t20   |   true    |
> +---------+-------------+---------+-----------+
>

query 'CALL rql::explain("from test::t20 map {id, a: cast(a, int8)} filter {a == 1}")'
---
> +-------+---------+----------+-------------+----------------------+
> |  idx  |  depth  |  parent  |    kind     |        detail        |
> +-------+---------+----------+-------------+----------------------+
> |   0   |    0    |   none   |   Filter    |  (a == Constant(1))  |
> |   1   |    1    |    0     |     Map     |      id, a as a      |
> |   2   |    2    |    1     |  TableScan  |      test::t20       |
> +-------+---------+----------+-------------+----------------------+
>
